WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Chad Lindberg: And then you feel it.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.280
I can always feel…

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.049
there will be like a hush behind me, you know
what I mean?

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:08.940
People will be talking and there will be this
hush and you feel that people are saying something

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.150
about you.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.820
And especially now, people can get on their
phones and they’ll be like “Hey, Chad?

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.510
Your name is Chad, right?”

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.949
and I’ll be like “Yeah…you’ve got
your phone, right.”

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:25.500
Film Courage: I know this is like a weird,
creepy question but are you a people watcher?

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.760
I don’t mean like…[laughs] I know this
can be taken so many ways…but…

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.630
Chad Lindberg: I love people! [Laughs] Film
Courage: I know this can be taken so many

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.880
ways but in terms of studying human nature?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.880
Chad Lindberg: Yeah.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.980
Film Courage: Observing people is what I meant…

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.430
Chad Lindberg: Yeah.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.460
I am an observer.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.460
I’m the guy who will be on the wall at the
party watching.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.580
I’m not the guy who will be like “Hey,
everybody!”

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.750
I watch people.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.940
And now it’s tricky when they watch you.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.550
So it’s kind of an interesting dichotomy…is
that right?

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.580
Is that the right word, dichotomy?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.580
It sounds right.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.580
Use it!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.580
Go for it.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.580
Film Courage: It sounds right.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.580
It sounds really good.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:08.890
Chad Lindberg: Yes, but it’s interesting
when once fame sort of enters the picture,

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.100
then you have people staring at you.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.220
So it makes it interesting.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.390
Film Courage: Right.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.250
For the times that maybe you feel you can
blend in more (which probably is not often)…like

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:26.880
let’s suppose you have a hat on or you just
feel you’re in a space where no one is too

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.400
celebrity focused, maybe in another town or
something.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.750
What catches your eye about people in terms
of character study?

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.110
Because for me, I’ll see people at the grocery
store and [my focus] it will be on the person

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.440
who may not be that glamorous but they are
busy doing their own thing and I’ll be like

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.740
zeroed on on them.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.740
Chad Lindberg: Totally.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:52.130
The people who have like interesting tics
or walks or they have a disability, you know?

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:58.700
I’m fascinated by how they operate with
life and how they’re interact with people.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.850
So I’ll really zero in on that because it’s
something.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.950
I don’t know.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.800
But yeah…people do catch my eye and then
I’ll try not to stare because it’s rude

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.570
to stare but I want to know.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:16.069
And a lot of those things I have brought in
to different characters.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.569
I’ll see someone doing something and I’ll
remember it from years ago and I’ll be like

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:21.980
“Okay, that might work for this [role].”

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.750
Observing is key to acting, you know?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:33.600
Film Courage: And on the flip side, when the
eyes are on you and maybe you’re in more

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.980
of a public setting, how does that feel?

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.930
Do you ever feel pressure to be superhuman
in some ways?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.640
Chad Lindberg: Yeah…you have to be…well
it depends on where it’s at.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:49.900
If you’re at an event where people are there
to see you, you know you’re on, you’re

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.200
present and it’s a beautiful thing.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.810
And then sometimes I will have my hat on somewhere
and I’m completely not even thinking about

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:03.330
it and someone will recognize you or it just
catches you off guard, you know?

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.181
And then you’re like “Wait, I am in the
public eye?”

00:03:06.181 --> 00:03:09.420
I have to remind myself because I’ll forget.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:16.520
Say like here in LA where it is kind of our
safe zone as actors in a way.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:22.480
But still I’ll be at the Ralph’s and Ralph’s
is a local grocery mart in Los Angeles.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.620
We love it here.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.630
But I’ll be there not thinking of it and
someone will say “Oh…wait…you’re…right?”

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:35.400
Because when you go out of Los Angeles that
is when people get really, really excited

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.200
because they don’t see celebrities all the
time.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:42.550
In LA we see everybody, you know?

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:43.709
And we’re sort of like Okay?

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:45.200
This is where ‘they’ live.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.940
And we respect that.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:50.599
But when you go outside of LA, that is when
people get really pumped.

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:53.370
Not to say that they don’t here but it’s
just a different thing.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.819
Film Courage: Right…just because today we’re
in this new age of camera phones and people

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:02.280
get in fights on subways, and instead of calling
the police, they just take their phone out.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:09.250
Do you feel any pressure that even if you’re
just at Ralph’s and you’re just looking

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:15.430
at the Rockstar [energy drinks] or whatever
and then you feel someone’s presence, do

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.049
you feel a little more self-conscious?

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:19.940
Chad Lindberg: Absolutely.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.319
It does make you feel self-conscious when
someone is sitting there kind of…and I always

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:31.400
feel it whenever I go into some place now
because of being recognizable I will sort

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:38.990
of case the place before…I’ll go in somewhere
and be like “Okay, this person will probably

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:39.990
recognize me.”

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:40.990
And then you feel it.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:41.990
I can always feel…

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.650
there will be like a hush behind me, you know
what I mean?

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:48.589
People will be talking and you feel this hush
and you know that they are saying something

00:04:48.589 --> 00:04:49.809
about you.

00:04:49.809 --> 00:04:54.479
And especially now, people can get on their
phones and they’ll be like “Hey, Chad?

00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:56.169
Your name is Chad, right?”

00:04:56.169 --> 00:04:59.680
and I’ll be like “Yeah…you’ve got
your phone, right.”

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.129
Back in the day it was like “Hey, Jesse!

00:05:02.129 --> 00:05:04.930
Hey, Ash!” and I still get that a lot.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:09.860
But now with the phones people can just go
in and type your name right away and figure

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:10.970
out who you are.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:16.089
On the flip side, I think these [holds up
his camera phone] are weapons to.

00:05:16.089 --> 00:05:20.710
We do have to be careful in these times because
I have had plenty of people all of the sudden

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:24.339
[holds his phone right up as if in another’s
face] just do this to me and I’m like “Do

00:05:24.339 --> 00:05:26.240
you want a photo?” [and they’ll say] “Yeah,
yeah, yeah.”

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.080
[And Chad responds] “Well how about you
get in the picture and how about I take the

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.280
photo and we’ll both be in it?”

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:38.349
Fame is an interesting thing to watch people’s…how
they react to it.

00:05:38.349 --> 00:05:43.419
It’s almost like some people can chill and
be cool and some people lose their bodily

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:44.449
functions.

00:05:44.449 --> 00:05:49.990
It’s fascinating to watch.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:54.939
And then some people will have a conversation
about you and they will be just as close as

00:05:54.939 --> 00:05:55.939
we are.

00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:59.050
And they will be talking as if you don’t
exist.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.439
Like you’re an object.

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:01.439
It’s fascinating.

00:06:01.439 --> 00:06:02.439
It’s fascinating.

00:06:02.439 --> 00:06:05.430
And I really try…I don’t take it personally,
you know what I mean?

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.849
I understand that is the inner workings of
fame and how it works and celebrity.

00:06:09.849 --> 00:06:16.759
But a lot of times it can be invasive sometimes,
you know?

00:06:16.759 --> 00:06:22.139
When people follow you into a restroom, you
know these things happen.

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:29.469
98 percent of the time it’s love and I feel
really, really fortunate to have been in projects

00:06:29.469 --> 00:06:37.119
that people know and recognize me and people
are recognizing your work and that’s great.

00:06:37.119 --> 00:06:41.139
Film Courage: I know I’ve heard Marc Maron
talk about how he could feel the room when

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:47.442
he went up on stage and tell what would be
a crowd that he could play to [as a comic]

00:06:47.442 --> 00:06:49.219
and they would love and then vice versa.

00:06:49.219 --> 00:06:53.059
And I think I’ve heard Nikki Sixx say the
same thing, he’s very sensitive to the energy

00:06:53.059 --> 00:06:54.059
around him.

00:06:54.059 --> 00:06:57.819
So when you feel that maybe the energy isn’t
totally friendly, do you leave?

00:06:57.819 --> 00:06:59.379
Chad Lindberg: I leave.

00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:00.379
I leave.

00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:06.910
I’ve been in plenty of situations where
people have wanted to fight me because I’m

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.110
famous.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:14.349
Because maybe there were people in the room
or a female that got excited and wanted a

00:07:14.349 --> 00:07:15.349
photo.

00:07:15.349 --> 00:07:21.789
And I’ve had several people over the years
want to come out and hurt me and I just (very

00:07:21.789 --> 00:07:25.490
cooly) be like “It’s not me that you’re
upset with here.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.349
It’s whatever you’ve got going on.

00:07:27.349 --> 00:07:29.180
And it’s cool and I’ll leave.”

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:33.289
I’m not going to stick around if someone
wants to challenge me.

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:41.949
Because “Hey Hollywood” I don’t put
up with it, so…but you know it happens.

00:07:41.949 --> 00:07:43.919
I always say fame is a double-edge sword.

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:47.279
Film Courage: Right…and I just have one
last question and we’ll move on because

00:07:47.279 --> 00:07:48.610
I feel like I’m grilling you.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:49.610
Chad Lindberg: No.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:50.610
It’s alright.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.889
Film Courage: When you felt that this [being
recognizable] change in your life because

00:07:53.889 --> 00:08:00.349
I’m sure in the beginning you could go places
and people didn’t have their agendas whether

00:08:00.349 --> 00:08:04.159
it was where they were in love with you or
jealous of you, whatever it was.

00:08:04.159 --> 00:08:06.969
But when you felt it shift, how was that for
you?

00:08:06.969 --> 00:08:12.259
Chad Lindberg: I remember the moment that
shifted and it was the day after The Fast

00:08:12.259 --> 00:08:13.669
and The Furious came out.

00:08:13.669 --> 00:08:18.409
We…my family and I had gone to see it in
a town near Seattle.

00:08:18.409 --> 00:08:24.930
And we went into the theater, we watched it
and then we came out and I got mauled by people.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.139
It was insane.

00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:27.639
And I was like “Whoa!”

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:35.500
Because I didn’t expect that movie…my
Mom asked me if we wanted to have a film premiere

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:39.680
for The Fast and The Furious back home and
I said…I go “Mom no one is ever going

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:46.210
to see this film” because I was ignorant,
I was very young and I didn’t understand…again

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.370
we go back to being young and sort of having
these big hits.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.820
You don’t realize what you have.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:57.350
And that movie taught me that you never, never
know.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:02.590
And I was so lucky to be a part of this huge
phenomenon.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:09.300
And to this day people recognize Jesse left
and right, so I’m really fortunate.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.820
And after I got mauled I went to another place
and got mauled again and then it just kept

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:22.320
happening and I remember at night…it freaked
me out so much and I was kind like…I was

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.980
crying…I was really upset and my Mom was
there and I’m like “Things have changed.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.390
Things have definitely changed.”

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:34.220
And it was a tearful joy but also scary because
it’s like “Whoa…”

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.330
You feel the shift.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:42.570
And it hasn’t been the same since and I’ve
learned to adjust and again I’m very thankful

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:46.650
for it, but it is an interesting position
to be in.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.940
Film Courage: I think a lot of people don’t
think about that.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:53.760
Because we’re in such an era of people wanting
to be famous whether it’s on Tumblr, Instagram,

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.160
Twitter, whatever but then there is this double-edge
sword.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:02.540
But then you know the Chad that was the little
boy in the second grade and you know a different

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.890
Chad then the way the world projects [fame
onto you].

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:10.110
So it’s got to be an interesting thing because
you know yourself as Chad the human and other

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.370
people see you as Chad the actor or as superhuman.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.580
Chad Lindberg: They do…a lot of people see
the perception, what they want to think of

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.580
you.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:23.880
It’s not who I am, just what they see and
what they sort of want to put in their little

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.380
box of what you are.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:28.400
And we do that I think with a lot of celebrities.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.250
We just truly don’t know.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:34.800
My favorite is when somebody says “So and
so is a jerk!”

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.110
I go “Really?

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:37.830
Have you ever met this person?”

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.360
I’m talking about celebrity.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.800
This celebrity that is a jerk.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.740
“Really have you ever met them?” [and
they respond] “No.” [and Chad responds]

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.510
Then you can never say that about this person.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.510
You can’t!

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:51.270
Because somebody out there is saying that
Chad Lindberg is an jerk because I looked

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.220
at them a certain way or I didn’t hear them.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.180
Am I a jerk?

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.180
No!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.340
So it’s interesting when people say that.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:03.570
I just think unless you know somebody in this
business, you don’t know them.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.800
Film Courage: Sure.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.130
Well I know Mickey Rourke was interviewed
and he said that LA was a town built on envy.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:15.260
And I think that is true in many ways and
so I think sometimes that a lot of it comes

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:18.410
from that because we wish we were in their
[a celebrity] shoes.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.410
But anyway…thank you!

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.410
Chad Lindberg: Sure.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.410
Thank you!

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.220
And I love hearing those stories from guys
that have been around doing this for years.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:30.110
I’ve been doing this a long time but he’s
been doing this a long time, too.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:31.570
It’s interesting to hear similar stories.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:32.790
Film Courage: Yeah.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.080
It was a Piers Morgan interview with Mickey
Rourke.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.080
And it was excellent.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.450
I highly recommend it.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.450
Okay.

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:39.450
Cool.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:40.450
So we’ll move on from here.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:41.450
Chad Lindberg: Awesome.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:41.463
Question for the viewers: Who is the nicest
celebrity you’ve met in person?

